// European pond turtle (Emys orbicularis): long-lived amphibious omnivore; hibernates in mud.
// Mass ≈ 0.5 kg, ≈ 40 yr, maturity ≈ 8 yr, 3–16 eggs incubated ≈ 75 d (AnAge, order of
// magnitude; `litter` = surviving hatchlings). The shell gives a high defence. Rig `turtle`.
// Water economy `food_water` 1.5: a reptile, but it lives in and drinks from ponds (designer).
